'''''Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: The Visual Dictionary''''' is a [[canon]] reference book for the film [[Star Wars: Episode IX The Rise of Skywalker|''Star Wars'': Episode IX ''The Rise of Skywalker'']]. The book was written by [[Pablo Hidalgo]] and published by [[Dorling Kindersley|DK Publishing]] on [[December 20]], [[2019]], the same day as the film itself.

==Publisher's summary==
''Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: The Visual Dictionary is a 200-page definitive guide to ''Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker'', revealing the characters, creatures, droids, locations, and technology from the new film. Packed with 500+ images and information, plus cross-sections of new vehicles, as penned by ''Star Wars'' scribe Pablo Hidalgo, it's a must-have for all fans who want to go beyond the movie experience.''

==Continuity==
*On page 91, the book alleges that [[Poe Dameron]] did not return home for five years after joining the [[Spice Runners of Kijimi]]. However, the novel ''[[Poe Dameron: Free Fall]]'' and reference book ''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' later narrowed down Dameron's time as a Spice Runner to one year.
*On page 104, the [[Festival of the Ancestors]] is stated to occur every two years when it really only occurs every forty-two years making this an error.

